+## Result summary (faithful to the researcher's final output, attributed not endorsed)
+
+- Question: is there a COMPACT, HUMAN-SURVEYABLE certificate for `S(12) > 29` (every
+  height-29 adaptive comparison tree on 12 labelled keys errs on some input) that does
+  not just reproduce the exhaustive poset search?
+- Answer horn (C), HONEST INCONCLUSIVE / strongly negative in practice: **no compact
+  human-readable certificate is known**. The established proof (Wells; Peczarski 2012;
+  Stober–Weiß 2023, arXiv:2206.05597v2, ALENEX) is the exhaustive admissible
+  forward/backward level search on `e(P)` (linear extensions). The reported `6190`
+  stored posets are search bookkeeping under a threshold parameter, NOT a small
+  hand-verifiable bottleneck family. Five scalar-invariant classes are already
+  falsified in the repo (`research-n12-nontightness.md` §5), and `m(P)` is not monotone
+  in `e(P)`, so low-dimensional potentials do not give a short certificate.
+- The agent's own scratch one-sided replay (`/tmp/opencode/s12_search.py`) was SIGKILLed
+  at level c≈2 (`|S_1|=66`, `|S_2|=1485`); it produced no new witness object and its
+  computation is NOT a verified reproduction of the search death level.
